{"author":{"id":"8022379585b4ab99ca8775db3eb67d33fcb256817114c28e51ccc1e9f55cdec4"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1792310790,"nonce":"Xha9vJGy52IZ0MwPUxaB8CKO3mA=","title":"BIGGEST WIN of the arc: prefill attention never ran in Haxe (every fast path gated seqQ==1), so it fell to the RUST bmm. Implemented ...","message":"ttft **2.814 / 2.796 / 2.812 s OFF** vs **0.931 / 1.077 / 0.924 s ON** = **-63% to\n-67%, ~2.7-3.0x**, 3/3. The OFF arm spreads 0.6% — this A/B is precise, it does\nnot need the server bench.\n\nGenerated text DIFFERS from the F32-prefill path at TEMP=0 (both coherent, both\non-topic) — expected, since greedy decoding turns one flipped logit into a\ndifferent continuation. That is NOT a defect (see below) but it also is not\nproof of equal quality. `grep -rl perplexity|logprob|crossEntropy nue/` returns\nNOTHING. **Next concrete step = build a top-1-agreement / perplexity harness\n(teacher-forced argmax over a fixed corpus, both paths), then flip the default\non a number rather than on two eyeballed samples.**\n\n`nue/tests/flashbatch` shows **decodeBatch row r == decode(cacheLen = baseLen +\nr + 1), BIT-IDENTICAL**: 46976 lanes, zero diffs, over MHA + GQA(14q/2kv),\nheadDim 64/128, baseLen 0 and non-zero, seqQ 1/8/16, workers 1/4/8. The test\nfalls out of the causal mask (K/V already resident ⇒ row r sees [0, baseLen+r])\nand compares against the SHIPPING single-row default, not the Rust bmm.\n\n**\"Not token-identical\" was never evidence of a defect.** The prefill fallback\nis the Rust bmm, which DEQUANTISES TO F32 — a different numeric path by\nconstruction. decodeBatch matches the Q8xQ8 path that already ships for decode.\nWhat remains before default-on is a QUALITY question, not a correctness one:\nprefill moves from F32 attention to Q8xQ8 attention, so check generated output\nend-to-end at TEMP=0 before flipping the default.\n\nEvery fast attention path in `GQAttention.forward` is gated on **`seqQ == 1`**\n(decode). A multi-token prompt therefore fell through to\n`bmm + scale + mask + softmax + bmm`, where both bmms are\n`Tensor.bmmThreaded` — a RUST extern on the RUST `worker_pool`. And\n`FlashDecode.decodeBatch` was a **stub** (`return null`, `batchMax()==1`, so its\nown gate `seqQ\u003e1 \u0026\u0026 seqQ\u003c=1` was unsatisfiable). Prefill attention had simply\nnever been ported; `RAYZOR_HAXE_FLASH=1` only ever enabled the DECODE kernel.\n\n`decodeBatch` over the Q8 cache. Query row `r` attends keys `[0, baseLen + r]`,\nso **the causal mask is just a per-row cache length** — no mask tensor, no\n`expandKvHeads` copies, no materialised `[heads, seqQ, cacheLen]` scores. Rows\nband across the SpinPool; scores/V scratch is indexed by the band's WORKER id;\nthe query quantiser is byte-identical to `decode`'s.\n\n\n    ttft  12.046s -\u003e 5.538s   and   12.518s -\u003e 6.295s     (-54% / -50%)\n    perf: rayzor_tensor_bmm_threaded 23.5% -\u003e ABSENT (\u003c1%)\n    band_ms RISES 6966 -\u003e 7493 — attention now runs ON the SpinPool and counts\n      toward that meter; the win is the deleted Rust bmm + handoff spin.\n\n**~2.2x prefill.** Larger than every inner-loop lever of this arc combined\n(six measured, all 1-5%).\n\n- Output is COHERENT but **not token-identical** to the Rust fallback. Expected:\n  this does Q8xQ8 attention (like decode), the fallback dequantises Q8-\u003eF32\n  first. **Numeric equivalence is NOT proven** — that gate is required before\n  default-on.\n- This file already carried a warning that a PRIOR `seqQ\u003e1` experiment\n  \"regressed full-model correctness\"; hence opt-in from a fresh implementation.\n- Shifted-Q form and the no-pool case return null (fall back).\n- Suggested next gate: force `seqQ==1` through `decodeBatch` and require\n  BIT-IDENTICAL output vs `decode`, which validates the per-row causal length\n  and offset plumbing against the proven kernel.\n\nI cached the env value with `_batchMax = -1` meaning unread. **A cross-module\nduplicate of a static starts at 0**, so `batchMax()` returned 0 and the path\nstayed silently disabled — and my first \"output is identical\" check was\nmeasuring the new code NEVER RUNNING. The neighbouring gates (`_enabled`,\n`_pool`) use 0-as-unread with 1/2 for on/off precisely for this, and the file\nsays so. Store `value + 1` for integer settings.\n**Always prove a new path EXECUTED (a gated print) before trusting an A/B.**\n\nA whole session of band-kernel inner-loop work returned 1-5% per lever, four of\nthem dead. ONE structural gap — a kernel that was never written — returned 2.2x.\n[[perf_prefill_profile_two_pools_idle_each_other]] is what found it, and only\nbecause I profiled instead of assuming the band kernel was the whole story.\n**Profile before optimising; \"where is the time\" beats \"make this part faster\".**\n\n---\nArchived from Claude memory `perf_haxe_batched_prefill_attention` on 2026-10-18. A record of past work; open items in it may have their own issues.","files":null}]}